{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "blitzconnect-all-001",
    "name": "QX BlitzConnect - All APIs",
    "description": "BlitzConnect REST collection: Authentication, Orders, Portfolio, Positions, Trades, Profile, Session, Signals, Strategy Statistics and Market Data.\n\nBEFORE YOU RUN\n0. Set {{appKey}} and {{userId}} - both ship blank so no secret is committed. Retarget any environment by changing {{baseURL}} alone; every other base URL is derived from it.\n\nHOW TO USE:\n1. Run '1.1 Login' first - it saves the JWT into {{authToken}} automatically.\n2. All other requests use Bearer {{authToken}} (set at collection level).\n3. Note the Market Data folder uses its own base URLs ({{mdApiBaseUrl}} and {{instrumentBaseUrl}}), not {{apiBaseUrl}}.\n\nWEBSOCKETS ARE NOT IN THIS COLLECTION - AND CANNOT BE.\nA Postman v2.1 collection cannot hold WebSocket requests alongside HTTP requests, and Postman cannot export WebSocket requests in v2.1 JSON at all. Any WebSocket entry in a v2.1 file always imports back as a plain HTTP GET, which is exactly what you would have seen in the folders that used to be numbered 10 and 11. Testing lives in a script instead:\n\n    python WebSocket-Test-Script.py --collection BlitzConnect.postman_collection.json\n\nIt reads the variables from this file, logs in, and exercises both sockets:\n  - Interactive   {{WsBaseUrl}}/api_interactive/ws?access_token=<JWT>\n    order, trade, position and statistics events as plain JSON. Sends a\n    plain-text 'ping' every 30s to keep the connection alive.\n  - Market Data   {{WsBaseUrl}}/md-streaming/ws?key=<JWT>\n    live ticks as base64-encoded protobuf. Note the parameter is key=,\n    not access_token=.\n\nKNOWN SERVER-SIDE ISSUE\n'10.5 Option Chain' returns HTTP 400 'Instrument not found for symbol NSECM|NIFTY' on UAT. This is a backend fault, reproduced on more than one environment - not a client or payload error. Confirm the expiry is current before assuming your own request shape is wrong.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "type": "string",
        "value": "{{authToken}}"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "appKey",
