    {
      "name": "10. Market Data",
      "description": "Market Data REST - instrument master and live/historical pricing. This is a **separate service** from the Interactive API: it uses `{{mdApiBaseUrl}}` for pricing and `{{instrumentBaseUrl}}` for instrument lookups, not `{{apiBaseUrl}}`. Same Bearer token and same `1.1 Login`.\n\nFor streaming prices instead of polling, use `WebSocket-Test-Script.py` - see the collection description for why streaming is not in Postman.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "10.1 Instrument Details by ID",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{instrumentBaseUrl}}/{{instrumentId}}",
              "host": ["{{instrumentBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["{{instrumentId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Full instrument master record by numeric id: `instrumentId`, `symbol`, `ticker`, `exchangeSegment`, `instrumentType`, `lotSize`, `tickSize`, `freezeQty`, `isin`, price band, and OHLC + `ltp`.\n\nVerified in UAT - returns HTTP 200."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "10.2 Instrument Details by Symbol",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{instrumentBaseUrl}}/{{instrumentSymbol}}",
              "host": ["{{instrumentBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["{{instrumentSymbol}}"]
            },
            "description": "Same record, looked up by symbol.\n\n**The path segment must be `EXCHANGE_SEGMENT:SYMBOL`** - for example `NSECM:IDEA`. This was verified in UAT: a bare `IDEA` returns **HTTP 204 with an empty body**, not an error, which is easy to mistake for success. `NSEFO:IDEA` and `NSE:IDEA` also return 204; the segment has to match the instrument's own record.\n\nThe Python SDK hides this by accepting `NSECM|IDEA` and rewriting `|` to `:` for you."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "10.3 LTP (Last Traded Price)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{mdApiBaseUrl}}/marketfeed/ltp",
              "host": ["{{mdApiBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["marketfeed", "ltp"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"InstrumentIds\": [{{instrumentId}}]\n}"
            },
            "description": "Last traded price for one or more instruments. Cheapest way to smoke-test connectivity.\n\nResponse keys are **stringified instrument ids**: `{\"data\":{\"110010000002885\":{\"instrumentId\":...,\"ltp\":13.02}}}`.\n\nVerified in UAT - returns HTTP 200."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "10.4 Market Quote",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{mdApiBaseUrl}}/marketfeed/quote",
              "host": ["{{mdApiBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["marketfeed", "quote"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"InstrumentIds\": [{{instrumentId}}]\n}"
            },
            "description": "Full depth quote: `ltp`, `ltq`, `atp`, `vtt`, `tbq`, `tsq`, `oi`, OHLC, and five levels each of `bidLevel` and `askLevel` (index, price, quantity, orders).\n\nVerified in UAT - returns HTTP 200."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "10.5 Option Chain",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{mdApiBaseUrl}}/marketfeed/optionchain",
              "host": ["{{mdApiBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["marketfeed", "optionchain"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"Symbol\": \"{{instrumentSymbol}}\",\n  \"ExpiryDate\": \"{{expiryDate}}\",\n  \"ExchangeSegment\": 1,\n  \"InstrumentId\": {{instrumentId}}\n}"
            },
            "description": "All strikes for one underlying and expiry.\n\n**`ExpiryDate` is required** - omitting it returns HTTP 400 with `{\"errors\":{\"ExpiryDate\":[\"The ExpiryDate field is required.\"]}}`.\n\n> **This endpoint does not currently return 200 in UAT.** Every symbol form was tried against a live instrument list (145,297 instruments, with RELIANCE and NIFTY options listed to 2026-12-29): bare symbol, `NSECM:SYMBOL`, `NSEFO:SYMBOL`, both `optionchain` and `optionChain` path casings, camelCase and PascalCase bodies, with and without `InstrumentId`. All return HTTP 400 `Instrument not found for symbol <x>`. Routing and model validation clearly work, so the failure is in the server's symbol resolution rather than the request shape - worth raising with the backend. The C# SDK works around it by retrying the other path casing, which also did not help.\n\nThe body below is the shape the SDK and the server's own tests use."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "10.6 Historical Data",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{mdApiBaseUrl}}/marketfeed/historicalData",
              "host": ["{{mdApiBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["marketfeed", "historicalData"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"Instrument\": \"{{historicalSymbol}}\",\n  \"interval\": \"{{historicalInterval}}\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "OHLCV candles, newest first. Note the mixed casing in the field names: `Instrument` is capitalised, `interval` is **lower-case**. ASP.NET binds case-insensitively so both work, but match the SDK to avoid surprises.\n\n`timestamp` comes back as `\"30-09-2026 00:00:00\"` - `dd-MM-yyyy`, not ISO.\n\nVerified in UAT - returns HTTP 200."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
